WEBVTT

NOTE
login — 3 screens, 3 avatar scenes
ski-demo, BCP admin.

The shared sign-in opening, recorded on its own so it can be dropped over the front of every other BCP video. It ENDS settled on the dashboard — where each of those videos' third screen begins — and has no logout, which is footage the piece it replaces does not have.

EVERY SCENE HAS A LEAD-IN AND AN EXIT PAUSE.

  lead-in  0.5s   Sarah on screen before she starts. A scene that opens
                mid-word has no edit point.
  exit     0.8s   after she stops — the join the next scene's crossfade
                eats into, and what an editor trims to.

  A scene is lead-in + speech + exit. The cue covers ONLY the speech;
  the scene's own start and end are in its NOTE.

THE CUE TIMES ARE THE NARRATION TIMELINE, not the footage. The `raw` line
in each NOTE is how long that screen was really on camera. They differ on
purpose — a screen that takes 15 seconds to fill in does not need 15
seconds of talking over it. What matters is that no screen is SHORTER
than its scene.

SPEAKING RATE 3.44 words a second. MEASURED, from two rendered clips —
31 words in 9.01s, see 01-first-time-ordering/script_v33.json's _wps_note.
